Select the numerical value that correctly answers the following problem.

The shared integer x is initially 0. Three threads execute exactly once:
```text
A: rA = x;  x = 2*rA + 1;
B: rB = x;  x = rB + 3;
C: rC = x;  x = rC + 5;
```
Each displayed read and each displayed write is separately atomic. Local registers are private. Execution is sequentially consistent, and a thread's read precedes its write. After all six operations have completed, how many distinct final values of x are possible?

Select the numerical value that correctly answers the following problem.

Starting with one process, the following code executes. Every fork succeeds, returns 0 only in its new child, and returns a positive child identifier in its parent. Every process reaches the final line once. How many processes execute work()?

```c
int p = fork();
if (p == 0) fork();
fork();
work();
```

**Required precision:** Integer.

Select the numerical value that correctly answers the following problem.

A lexically scoped language permits variable shadowing. In the code below, each declaration introduces a distinct variable and declarations take effect immediately. How many distinct declared variables are referenced by the three print expressions, collectively?

```text
var x;
var y;
{
    var x;
    print(x);
    {
        var y;
        print(x + y);
    }
    print(y);
}
```

**Required precision:** Integer.

Select the numerical value that correctly answers the following problem.

What integer is printed? The static variable is initialized once.

```c
#include <stdio.h>
int f(int n) {
    static int k = 0;
    int a = ++k;
    if (n == 0) return a;
    return a + f(n-1);
}
int main(void) {
    int x = f(2);
    int y = f(1);
    printf("%d\n", x+y);
    return 0;
}
```

**Required precision:** Integer.

Select the numerical value that correctly answers the following problem.

What integer is printed by this conforming C program?

```c
#include <stdio.h>
struct S { int a[2]; int *p; };
int main(void) {
    struct S s = {{1,2}, 0};
    s.p = s.a;
    struct S t = s;
    t.a[0] = 7;
    *t.p = 9;
    printf("%d\n", s.a[0] + t.a[0]);
    return 0;
}
```

**Required precision:** Integer.

Select the numerical value that correctly answers the following problem.

What integer does this conforming C program print? Each recursive call shares the same pointed-to integer.

```c
#include <stdio.h>
int f(int n, int *p) {
    if (n == 0) return *p;
    *p += n;
    int a = f(n-1, p);
    *p -= 1;
    return a + *p;
}
int main(void) {
    int x = 1;
    printf("%d\n", f(3, &x));
    return 0;
}
```

**Required precision:** Integer.

Select the numerical value that correctly answers the following problem.

What does this conforming C program print?

```c
#include <stdio.h>
void change(int **q, int *r) {
    **q += 2;
    *q = r;
    **q += 3;
}
int main(void) {
    int a = 4, b = 7;
    int *p = &a;
    change(&p, &b);
    printf("%d\n", a + b + *p);
    return 0;
}
```

**Required precision:** Integer.

Select the numerical value that correctly answers the following problem.

What integer is printed by this C code? All operations are within the array.

```c
int a[] = {2,4,6};
int *p = a;
int x = *p++;
int y = ++*p;
printf("%d", x + y + a[1]);
```

**Required precision:** Integer.

Select the numerical value that correctly answers the following problem.

What integer is printed? All pointed-to objects remain alive.

```c
void change(int **p, int *q) {
    **p += 2;
    *p = q;
    **p += 3;
}
/* Inside main: */
int x=4, y=7;
int *p=&x;
change(&p, &y);
printf("%d", x+y+*p);
```

**Required precision:** Integer.

Select the numerical value that correctly answers the following problem.

A BST stores keys 1–15 in a perfectly balanced shape: root 8, recursively choosing the midpoint as each subtree root. Run this range-search procedure with lo=6, hi=10. Count non-null calls, including calls on nodes whose keys are not reported.

```text
search(node):
    if node is null: return
    if node.key > lo: search(node.left)
    if lo <= node.key <= hi: report(node.key)
    if node.key < hi: search(node.right)
```

**Required precision:** Integer.

Select the numerical value that correctly answers the following problem.

Assume conventional C semantics and representable integer values. What is the final value of a[1]?

```c
int a[3] = {1,2,3};
int *p = a;
int x = *p++;
*p += x;
```

**Required precision:** Integer.

Select the numerical value that correctly answers the following problem.

Assume all array accesses in this C program are valid and int can represent all values shown. What value is returned?

```c
int f(void) {
    int a[4] = {3, 5, 7, 9};
    int *p = a + 1;
    int **q = &p;
    (*q)++;
    **q += a[0];
    return p[-1] + a[2] + (int)(p - a);
}
```

**Required precision:** Exact integer.

Select the numerical value that correctly answers the following problem.

Initially one single-threaded process executes the following pseudocode. Every fork succeeds; a child returns0 from fork, and the parent returns a positive value. No process exits early.

```text
x = fork();
if x == 0 {
    fork();
} else {
    fork();
    fork();
}
```

How many processes, including the original, reach the end?

**Required precision:** Exact integer.

Select the numerical value that correctly answers the following problem.

Shared x initially equals0. Two threads each execute this sequence once, using the same binary semaphore mutex initially1:

```text
wait(mutex);
t = x;          // t is local to the thread
x = t + 1;
signal(mutex);
```

A third thread performs only wait(mutex); signal(mutex). All three threads finish successfully. How many distinct final values of x are possible?

**Required precision:** Exact integer.

Select the numerical value that correctly answers the following problem.

At the exit of the following straight-line block, only r is live. Assignments are evaluated sequentially.

```text
a=b+c;
d=a+e;
a=f;
r=d+a;
```

How many distinct variables are live at block entry?

**Required precision:** Exact integer.
